      "reviewReasons": {
        "requirements": "All seven ACs are covered by the spec and the diff, including the 'überfällig' wording and the 'nur überfällige' control. The first spec version mistakenly capitalised 'Überfällig' and left out the filter, and only a later update corrected both.",
        "scope": "The change adds an unrequested error paragraph and a loading-disable mechanism in the UI, and it commits a large plan document to docs/. The strict overdue query validation and the retry behaviour are also additions beyond the ACs.",
        "tests": "The API and store tests are thorough: UTC boundaries, validation, atomic patches, filter cases and order. There are no automated UI tests, and an existing test was only updated for the new fields, not weakened.",
        "conventions": "The change uses ValidationError mapped to 400, Node builtins only, data-testid attributes and TDD-style tests. The new elements follow existing idioms, and the plan document is extra repository clutter.",
        "architecture": "Validation and the overdue computation live in the store, and the HTTP layer only filters and maps errors. The date logic is slightly duplicated in the test and snapshot code, and snapshot defaults today per call.",
        "codeQuality": "Patches are applied atomically and the date round-trip validation is strict and correct. Minor issues: a null input to add() would throw a TypeError, and the page's top-level await makes the UI code a bit heavier than needed."
      },
